                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d9a59e26-d1cd-3017-9bc2-43afe4ff3136",
                        "entry_id": "484f16c9-cdd5-3e1f-a76b-7094381d7e31",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having characteristics similar to those of a bat, usually used with reference to the flying mammal."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "af415940-f159-41f3-ba0c-34711059ef15",
                                "sense_id": "d9a59e26-d1cd-3017-9bc2-43afe4ff3136",
                                "text": "[…] they cling, like creepers or women, to the nearest support, to fly from that corroding ennui and listlessness, those tumults of the mind, which flit batlike amid the golden-groined ceilings, and cannot be dispelled by the lictor guard."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e7732422-6759-4289-840d-b7ec57c72d64",
                                "sense_id": "d9a59e26-d1cd-3017-9bc2-43afe4ff3136",
                                "text": "He had told himself bitterly as he walked through the streets that she was a figure of the womanhood of her country, a batlike soul waking to the consciousness of itself in darkness and secrecy and loneliness."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c70174ce-65f6-4740-a8fe-eff497bda5b2",
                                "sense_id": "d9a59e26-d1cd-3017-9bc2-43afe4ff3136",
                                "text": "There was a trap somewhere, I felt sure; and though I didn't know the term \"hush-money,\" its meaning flittered, bat-like, about my mind."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8333136f-90d5-477d-a3de-4bd9585b734c",
                                "sense_id": "d9a59e26-d1cd-3017-9bc2-43afe4ff3136",
                                "text": "The most famous of these Los Caprichos is “The Sleep of Reason Produces Monsters” (plate 43), which has a sky full of batlike creatures."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a5f586ac-51be-3bb0-96cd-ae7a0d08acb8",
                        "entry_id": "484f16c9-cdd5-3e1f-a76b-7094381d7e31",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Similar to that of a bat."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "22b46223-5b98-4958-a80b-f29f3ff3cdb7",
                                "sense_id": "a5f586ac-51be-3bb0-96cd-ae7a0d08acb8",
                                "text": "His sketches show the details of batlike wings which were to spread out on the downward stroke and fold up with the upward stroke."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cfd1afcf-3ea7-4f80-a7f7-91c8ca78ee21",
                                "sense_id": "a5f586ac-51be-3bb0-96cd-ae7a0d08acb8",
                                "text": "What was it? They could not tell themselves. They only knew that the black shadows at the top of the staircase had thickened, had coalesced, had taken a definite, batlike shape."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a4223996-2e9d-4bdd-bf3c-7527e5131879",
                                "sense_id": "a5f586ac-51be-3bb0-96cd-ae7a0d08acb8",
                                "text": "The Oilbird is one of the few bird species to use batlike echolocation to help navigate the night and cave darkness."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
